  "about": "What fills each room type, from existing parts (docs/sandbox/INTERIORS.md). Items are placed one to a floor slab's free socket, inside first. count: how many; perCells: one more every N cells of floor; loot: true fills it from the room's loot hook; role: what it is for (helm, gunner, engineer...). missing: what the room should have that no part does yet (printed by the run, never invented). The shell (walls, floors, stairs, doors) is in 'shell'; its 'panels' are long walls with few links, longest first, for straight runs of plain wall (phase 5). A part may be a list, biggest size class first: the builder takes the first the vehicle's class allows (SizeClasses.json partClass) that fits a room's block (2.5 m high, 3.6 m across), a bigger one on the shell's adapter pad. feeds: links laid from another room's things into this room's (a chute from storage into the Assembler, a pipe from a fuel bunker's tank into the plant), at ceiling height, from the nearest within reach (phase 8).",
